{"id": "get_user_head_explicit", "group": "methods", "method": "HEAD", "path": "/users/1", "headers": {}, "body": null, "fastapi_doc": "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/path-params/", "expect_status": 200, "expect_body_empty": true, "notes": "Confirmed live and deliberately left unmatched in the reference (fastapi_app.py has no @app.head for /users/{id}): quackapi answers HEAD on any GET route automatically, with no explicit registration; bare Starlette does not (405 there without an explicit HEAD decorator, confirmed by running the pinned reference). quackapi does more than plain FastAPI here — a real divergence to surface, not a gap to paper over. The prior NOT-BUILT-YET label had it backwards.", "class_hint": "STRONGER"}
